  "loc": "Section 1 Introduction, p. 4",
  "quote": "we study the auditability properties of mechanisms for allocation problems without money",
  "note": "The main object is the auditability (detectability of deviations) of object allocation mechanisms: priority-based allocation/school choice (DA, IA, AR) and house allocation (hierarchical exchange, TTC, sequential dictatorships). This is matching/allocation, not collective decision by voting. Binary-outcome voting appears only as one secondary application in Appendix A.3 (alongside auctions and affirmative-action choice). Coding stopped per codebook."
